  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.56",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\ell(X)$ denote the composition length of a finite group $X$. Let $A$ be a finite nilpotent group acting by automorphisms on a finite soluble group $G$. Let $c(G,A)$ be the number of trivial $A$-modules in a given $A$-composition series of $G$. (Note that $c(G,A)=\\ell(C_G(A))$ if $(|A|,|G|)=1$.)\n\nConjecture: there are absolute constants $C_1$ and $C_2$ such that the Fitting height of $G$ is at most $C_1\\ell(A)+C_2c(G,A)$.",
